{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/994466-defensive-rotes","id":994466,"title":"Defensive Rotes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-28T01:52:01-07:00","id":994466,"title":"Defensive Rotes","content":"So, I'm playing a cross-over, there're mages,garou, vampires, hunters, demons and whatnot.<br /> Lately my mage has been getting the attention of various individuals, unwillingly, and I get ambushed rather frequently.<br /> <br /> My mage has 5 arete, corresp 3,forces 4 ,spirit 2 ,prime 3 and life 3<br /> <br /> What defenses could I use to protect myself from sudden ambushes with ranged weapons such as snipers, or even closed ranged physical attacks, such as someone trying to slice my head off with a katana and so on lol..<br /> I thought about casting a kinetic shield with forces 2 on myself, everyday and subtracting successes inorder to make it last for the whole day, so any physical attacks at all would be blocked or considerably weakened, however such a defense is a bit too vulgar so I was wondering if there's anything else I could do to protect my mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T02:14:16-07:00","id":994470,"title":"","content":"Inspired by a new Obfuscate 6 entry from the new Vampire Lore Of The Clans book (Page 163):<br /> <br /> Use Forces 2 to bend light, causing you to be slightly (and dynamically) displaced visually. This increases the attack difficulty against yourself as most attacks just 'barely miss'. Perception+Awareness can be used to notice the effect and adjust aim, but the numbers need to be ST-decided on in mage terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T03:19:23-07:00","id":994477,"title":"","content":"An obvious one would be to make yourself an invisible prime shield around your body. giving you soak for Agg damage. With life 3 you could even make this shield a part of your Skin's pattern. Though you'll need ST approval.<br /> It won't stop you getting hit, but you'll need it if you're going toe to toe with a Garou, even just to survive long enough to escape.<br /> <br /> You can also use Spirit to make a LOT of friends in the spirit world, and I mean a LOT! If you get a good reputation with a select number, certain tribes will be more or less contractually obligated to leave you alone. Not easy though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T03:20:34-07:00","id":994478,"title":"","content":"I'd try to get Mind 1 ASAP.<br /> <br /> Correspondence 3 + Mind 1 lets you expand your senses considerably and sense hostile intent as you do, and Mind 1 also makes it simple to comprehend such a massive amount of information.<br /> <br /> You've got plenty of in-character reasons from the sound of it to justify being paranoid enough to be scanning a few blocks around you for ambushes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T03:22:05-07:00","id":994479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/994466-defensive-rotes?p=994470#post994470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Inspired by a new Obfuscate 6 entry from the new Vampire Lore Of The Clans book (Page 163):<br /> <br /> Use Forces 2 to bend light, causing you to be slightly (and dynamically) displaced visually. This increases the attack difficulty against yourself as most attacks just 'barely miss'. Perception+Awareness can be used to notice the effect and adjust aim, but the numbers need to be ST-decided on in mage terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it pretty much the same as Slipstream? (Corresp 2) <br /> Also, if it makes everyone attack me at the difficulty of 10 for an example, wouldnt it be pretty vulgar? idk","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12376-mowtekpvp","name":"MowtekPvP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T04:06:15-07:00","id":994488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MowtekPvP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/994466-defensive-rotes?p=994479#post994479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it pretty much the same as Slipstream? (Corresp 2) <br /> Also, if it makes everyone attack me at the difficulty of 10 for an example, wouldnt it be pretty vulgar? idk</div> </div> </div> </div>It is pretty much the same using a different sphere for the mahick enhancing ability portion of the mechanics.<br /> Vulgarity is not a matter of difficulty. And the maximum net modifier (according to m20) is 3. So most attacks would go against 9.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:21:35-07:00","id":994778,"title":"","content":"What's your Paradigm? and I can come up with more flavourful possibilites","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:43:10-07:00","id":994796,"title":"","content":"Get time one and mind one, and with correspondence 1 you can make a &quot;never get caught off guard, always go first&quot; rote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1552-asssassin","name":"Asssassin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T07:45:33-07:00","id":995633,"title":"","content":"Correspondance 2/3, Forces 2/3. Move any kinetic based attacks to a previously determined location, or switch it around so the enemy takes the damage instead of you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T12:54:05-07:00","id":997839,"title":"","content":"Life 3 to soak agg and Forces 1 or 2 can increase the difficulty of attacks against you by 3. That should be enough, if you want more, increase your stamina with Life 3, or just your soak pool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T14:05:26-07:00","id":997876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/994466-defensive-rotes?p=995633#post995633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correspondance 2/3, Forces 2/3. Move any kinetic based attacks to a previously determined location, or switch it around so the enemy takes the damage instead of you.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Could you please elaborate a little bit further? I created a post here in the mage's forum asking for a rote to do something similar, the thing is, the mage in the case is a hermetic flambeau of dark ages mage, how wold you think such a spell could work within the DA:M hermetic paradigm? How much damage would it be able to revert to the attacker etc? <br /> Thanks in advance.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T14:41:55-07:00","id":997890,"title":"","content":"Roll some low level Correspondence, for full awareness of your surroundings, thus minimizing the great effect the possibility of getting ambushed (physically). Combined with Life and you can be aware of all living things around you, subtract out all life signs that you're expecting and you can make assumptions about the rest.<br /> <br /> Get some Life buffs going! Increase Stamina and Dexterity to avoid and reduce damage, but don't keep it on too long so as to avoid Patter Bleed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T15:39:07-07:00","id":997915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/994466-defensive-rotes?p=997876#post997876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Could you please elaborate a little bit further? I created a post here in the mage's forum asking for a rote to do something similar, the thing is, the mage in the case is a hermetic flambeau of dark ages mage, how wold you think such a spell could work within the DA:M hermetic paradigm? How much damage would it be able to revert to the attacker etc?<br /> Thanks in advance.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The short answer is that Hermetics don't deal well with Space magick and i'm not invested enough to dig deep into the paradim enough to answer that.<br /> <br /> the long answer im sure can be provided by JustJohn here.<br /> <br /> I do think i can help you with the second part of my previous post though. Use Vires 2 or 3 (cant remember which, but im leaning towards 3) and either Anima or Corona (or Primus for that matter) at 2 or 3. Anima 3 to translate the kinetic force to either strengthen your life pattern (extra health) or hurt the opponents (straight up damage), Corona 3 or 4 to assault their senses or Primus 4 or 5 to assault their Quintessence pool.<br /> Hermetics iirc use sympatetic links to do this kind or transference, by creating a connection between yourself and the recipient of your spell. This can be accomplished by either learning their True Name or inscribing something on either the person or on an object placed on that person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-03T17:20:43-07:00","id":997969,"title":"","content":"<br /> I think with forces and correspondence combined you could have a probably-not vulgar effect of hits knocking you around rather than going through you. <br /> EG badguy hits your arm with a baseball bat. Hard.<br /> Rather than breaking your arm, your entire self moves with the bat, minimizing damage. You might fall over or something, but maybe you'll bounce off the floor easier too. <br /> It might get vulgar when they're using blades or guns, so maybe if you combine it with life, you can have it so that they do a limited amount of damage that you can soak, but the rest causes you to move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}